{"files": [{"id": 65792586, "name": "2024-1477.pdf", "size": 536918, "is_link_only": false, "download_url": "https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/65792586", "supplied_md5": "22797b9c1701768500e56d1ab2faf1ad", "computed_md5": "22797b9c1701768500e56d1ab2faf1ad", "mimetype": "application/pdf"}], "folder_structure": {}, "authors": [{"id": 17288467, "full_name": "Nico D\u00f6ttling", "first_name": "Nico", "last_name": "D\u00f6ttling", "is_active": true, "url_name": "Nico_D_ttling", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 24269648, "full_name": "Gennaro Avitabile", "first_name": "Gennaro", "last_name": "Avitabile", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 17433465, "full_name": "Bernardo Magri", "first_name": "Bernardo", "last_name": "Magri", "is_active": false, "url_name": "Bernardo_Magri", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 6920750, "full_name": "Christos Sakkas", "first_name": "Christos", "last_name": "Sakkas", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 17287906, "full_name": "Stella Wohnig", "first_name": "Stella", "last_name": "Wohnig", "is_active": false, "url_name": "Stella_Wohnig", "orcid_id": ""}], "custom_fields": [], "figshare_url": "https://publications.cispa.de/articles/conference_contribution/Signature-based_Witness_Encryption_with_Compact_Ciphertext/32771082", "download_disabled": false, "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\">Signature-based witness encryption (SWE) is a recently proposed notion that allows to encrypt a message with respect to a tag T and a set of signature verification keys. The resulting ciphertext can only be decrypted by a party who holds at least k different valid signatures w.r.t. T and k different verification keys out of the n keys specified at encryption time. Natural applications of this primitive involve distributed settings (e.g., blockchains), where multiple parties sign predictable messages, such as polling or randomness beacons. However, known SWE schemes without trusted setup have ciphertexts that scale linearly in the number of verification keys. This quickly becomes a major bottleneck as the system gets more distributed and the number of parties increases. Towards showing the feasibility of SWE with ciphertext size sub-linear in the number of keys, we give a construction based on indistinguishability obfuscation (iO) for Turing machines and strongly puncturable signatures (SPS).</p>", "funding": "ERC PICOCRYPT 101001283", "funding_list": [{"id": 30307737, "title": "ERC PICOCRYPT 101001283", "grant_code": "", "funder_name": null, "is_user_defined": 1}, {"id": 28581566, "title": "Ensuring the security, scalability, and functionality of digital source systems", "grant_code": "TED2021-132464B-I00", "funder_name": null, "is_user_defined": 0, "url": "https://app.dimensions.ai/details/grant/grant.14856792"}, {"id": 28605374, "title": "EFFICIENT AND SECURE DATA PROTECTION AGAINST DIGITAL ATTACKS", "grant_code": "PID2022-142290OB-I00", "funder_name": null, "is_user_defined": 0, "url": "https://app.dimensions.ai/details/grant/grant.14864728"}, {"id": 30307623, "title": "ERC LACONIC 101041207", "grant_code": "", "funder_name": null, "is_user_defined": 1}], "version": 1, "status": "public", "size": 536918, "created_date": "2026-06-23T13:31:54Z", "modified_date": "2026-06-23T13:31:54Z", "is_public": true, "is_confidential": false, "is_metadata_record": false, "confidential_reason": "", "metadata_reason": "", "license": {"value": 1, "name": "CC BY 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"}, "tags": ["Signature-based witness encryption", "compactness"], "keywords": ["Signature-based witness encryption", "compactness"], "categories": [{"id": 49240, "title": "Cryptography", "parent_id": 49237, "path": "/49135/49237/49240", "source_id": "460401", "taxonomy_id": 118}], "references": [], "has_linked_file": false, "citation": "D\u00f6ttling, Nico; Avitabile, Gennaro; Magri, Bernardo; Sakkas, Christos; Wohnig, Stella (2026). Signature-based Witness Encryption with Compact Ciphertext